4. Dominance / majorization analysis
====================================

This is especially important.

For two partitions a and b of the same S, define the usual dominance order:

a >= b

if for every r,

```
sum_{i=1}^r a_i >= sum_{i=1}^r b_i,
```

after sorting both in non-increasing order.

Test whether b(T) is monotone under this order.

Specifically test both possibilities:

A. If partition a dominates partition b, does

```
b(T_a) >= b(T_b)
```

always hold?

B. If partition a dominates partition b, does

```
b(T_a) <= b(T_b)
```

always hold?

Report every counterexample.

This is important because the earlier data suggest that simple "concentration" is not monotone.

